      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-12967",
      ":question/problem": "A bag contains a finite number of red, white, and blue balls. Consider the following scenarios:\n\n1. A ball is drawn from the bag and put into the bag again. A second ball is then drawn. Let $R_{1}$ be the event \"the first ball is red,\" and let $R_{2}$ be the event \"the second ball is red.\"\n2. A ball is drawn from the bag and set aside. A second ball is then drawn. Let $W$ be the event \"the first ball is white,\" and let $B$ be the event \"the second ball is blue.\"\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $R_{1}$ and $R_{2}$ are independent\n2. $W$ and $B$ are dependent\n3. $W$ and $B$ are independent"
    },
