      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-12968",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following scenarios:\n\n- A card is drawn from a standard $52$-card deck and put back into the deck. Then, a second card is drawn. Let $A_{1}$ be the event \"The first card is an Ace,\" and let $A_{2}$ be the event \"the second card is an Ace.\"\n- A card is drawn from a standard $52$-card deck and set aside. Then, a second card is drawn. Let $H_{1}$ be the event \"the first card is a heart,\" and $H_{2}$ be the event \"the second card is a heart.\"\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $A_{1}$ and $A_{2}$ are independent\n2. $A_{1}$ and $A_{2}$ are dependent\n3. $H_{1}$ and $H_{2}$ are independent"
    }
